      "content": "Wait, are you sure about that? I heard from a contact in the regional trade office that it's actually a bit of an old-school term of endearment used among close associates. They said it shows you're \"in the know\" rather than being an outsider. If I use it carefully, can't it actually help break the ice and make the negotiation smoother? I don't want to be too formal and stiff if I can avoid it.",
