      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Attempting to mitigate risk by framing an offensive term lightly is a very precarious strategy in diplomacy. Even as a \"lighthearted nod,\" tone and context are easily lost across language and cultural barriers, making accidental offense highly probable. To build a personal connection without risking misinterpretation, focus instead on sincerely complimenting a well-known cultural achievement or industry success of the region. This genuine praise establishes rapport while remaining professionally appropriate.",
